{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For</b> — figuratively, as though his days were set like smoke, in the manner of 'it is entirely like smoke, entirely.'" "<b>Like a brand</b> — two." "<b>And are burned</b> — like 'וחרה נחשתה' (and its bronze glowed), in the manner of 'from on high He sent fire into my bones.' For the abundance of His anger against His enemies seethed His body, until His bones — whose nature is cold — were burned."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {0 "The verse fragment כי דרך כלו כעשן כלו is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The phrase may be corrupt or elliptical.", 2 "The quotations 'וחרה נחשתה' and 'ממרום שלח אש בעצמותי' appear to be approximate biblical allusions (Ezekiel 24:11 and Lamentations 1:13 respectively) rather than exact citations; rendered as they stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:46.071259411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}